  "turns": [
    "<internal>\nThey asked for a draft only — no calendar tool call. Just show the wording.\n</internal>\n\n<message to=\"discord-main\">\nHere's a draft — nothing sent or scheduled yet.\n\n**Subject:** Design Review — 30 min\n\n**To:** dana@example.com\n\n**When:** Thursday 6 November 2026, 15:00–15:30 UTC\n\n---\n\nHi Dana,\n\nI'd like to set up a 30-minute design review on Thursday 6 November at 15:00 UTC. The goal is to walk through the current design together, gather your feedback, and agree on any changes before we move ahead.\n\nRough agenda:\n- Walkthrough of the current design (10 min)\n- Feedback and open questions (15 min)\n- Next steps and owners (5 min)\n\nIf that time doesn't suit, let me know what works and I'll move it.\n\nThanks,\nTestBot\n\n---\n\nTwo things worth confirming before I send anything: 6 November 2026 falls on a Friday, not a Thursday — I've written Thursday above assuming you meant this year's 6 November (2025, a Thursday). Tell me which year you want and I'll fix the day name. Also happy to adjust the tone or drop the agenda if you'd prefer something shorter.\n</message>",
    "<message to=\"discord-main\">\nDone — created `appt-new-5`: **Design Review (30 min)**, Friday 6 November 2026, 15:00 UTC, with dana@example.com invited. No conflicts on your calendar that day.\n\nOn the date question from my draft: 6 November 2025 is in the past, so I booked 2026-11-06, which is a **Friday**. The \"Thursday\" in my draft wording was wrong — use \"Friday 6 November\" if you send that text to Dana.\n\nOne limitation: the calendar tool only takes a start time, no duration, so the 30 minutes lives in the title rather than the event length. Tell me if you want it handled differently.\n</message>"
